{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized the high-risk coronary-intervention plus exertional chest tightness plus near-syncope pattern and directed immediate emergency evaluation, with workable transport and medication-reconciliation boundaries. However, the trajectory did not sufficiently elicit immediate syncope red flags/vitals and did not actively handle the incomplete-results gap by asking about ECG, troponin/cardiac markers, renal function, electrolytes, or vital signs. These are responsibility-chain omissions, but they were mitigated by urgent ED handoff and family arrival, so they are minor/moderate rather than serious. Under the frozen rubric, any minor/moderate responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite completed higher-order barrier navigation and misconception correction.",
